{"call_id":"call_RhCbolgkaSQ0IsxmbAg5Aqqt","process_id":"76326","turn_id":"019ca732-e077-79e0-a883-8af70c03460c","command":["/usr/bin/bash","-lc","kspec task start @01KJDQ1D --json"],"cwd":"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"kspec task start @01KJDQ1D --json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","stdout":"{\"success\":true,\"message\":\"Started task: 01KJDQ1D\",\"task\":{\"_ulid\":\"01KJDQ1DQMCBX32KDVWBJBF8W1\",\"slugs\":[],\"title\":\"ULID short ref ambiguity in batch operations: when two ULIDs share a prefix (e.g. 01KJ4SNE9 and 01KJ\",\"type\":\"task\",\"description\":\"ULID short ref ambiguity in batch operations: when two ULIDs share a prefix (e.g. 01KJ4SNE9 and 01KJ4SNEC), short refs like @01KJ4SNE fail. kspec already has a shortest-unique-ID utility — this should be used anywhere refs are displayed (triage list, task list, inbox list, promote result_ref, etc.) so that presented refs are always unambiguous and copy-pasteable into subsequent commands.\",\"spec_ref\":\"@batch-exec\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"blocked_by\":[],\"depends_on\":[],\"context\":[],\"priority\":3,\"tags\":[],\"vcs_refs\":[],\"session_id\":\"01KJKCGRAVN1BTZ611MX7EK5H3\",\"created_at\":\"2026-02-26T19:33:01.300Z\",\"started_at\":\"2026-03-01T02:22:52.837Z\",\"submitted_at\":\"2026-03-01T02:04:07.920Z\",\"notes\":[{\"_ulid\":\"01KJDQA0MV956KKZREMG980AE6\",\"created_at\":\"2026-02-26T19:37:42.812Z\",\"author\":\"@claude\",\"content\":\"ENRICHMENT — Standalone context for this task:\\n\\n**What**: When two ULIDs share a prefix (e.g., 01KJ4SNE9... and 01KJ4SNEC...), the default 8-character short ref `@01KJ4SNE` is ambiguous and fails to resolve. The `ReferenceIndex.shortUlid()` method (in `src/parser/refs.ts` line 310) already computes the minimum unique prefix, but many places in the codebase use a hardcoded `_ulid.slice(0, 8)` instead. There are 69 occurrences of `_ulid.slice(0, 8)` across 19 files.\\n\\n**Where**: All places that format ULID refs for display need to use `shortUlid()` instead of `_ulid.slice(0, 8)`. Key files with hardcoded slicing:\\n- `src/cli/commands/triage.ts` (14 occurrences) — triage list, record, act, get, start\\n- `src/cli/commands/inbox.ts` (9 occurrences) — inbox list, add, promote\\n- `src/cli/commands/item.ts` (6 occurrences) — item list, get, add\\n- `src/cli/commands/plan.ts` (9 occurrences) — plan list, get\\n- `src/cli/commands/search.ts` (4 occurrences) — search results\\n- `src/cli/commands/session/context.ts` (4 occurrences) — session context display\\n- `src/triage/actions.ts` (1 occurrence) — promote result ref\\n- `src/parser/validate.ts` (8 occurrences) — validation output\\n- Several other files with 1-3 occurrences each\\n\\nThe `ReferenceIndex` is already available in most of these contexts (it's built during `initContext()` or `buildIndexes()`).\\n\\n**How**:\\n1. For each file, replace `_ulid.slice(0, 8)` with `index.shortUlid(_ulid)` where a ReferenceIndex is in scope\\n2. For files where no index is available, either thread the index through or create a lightweight shortening utility\\n3. For triage records (which aren't indexed in the main ReferenceIndex), consider building a local index or a dedicated triage ULID shortener\\n4. Ensure that refs displayed by any list/get/result command are always copy-pasteable into subsequent commands without ambiguity\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- No occurrences of `_ulid.slice(0, 8)` remain in display-facing code paths\\n- All displayed refs (triage list, task list, inbox list, search results, promote result_ref, etc.) use `shortUlid()` or equivalent\\n- A test with two items sharing an 8-character ULID prefix shows that displayed refs are still unique and resolvable\",\"supersedes\":null},{\"_ulid\":\"01KJKHK2NRA76YCR98DKGTC5RR\",\"created_at\":\"2026-03-01T01:53:14.936Z\",\"author\":\"Jacob Chapel\",\"content\":\"Execution context:\\n- Background: displayed short refs currently use fixed 8-char ULID prefixes in many output paths; collisions make copy/paste refs ambiguous.\\n- Scope: update display-facing short-ref formatting to use shortest unique prefixes via ReferenceIndex (or equivalent local unique-set helper where index is unavailable) and add regression tests for ambiguous-prefix scenarios.\\n- Files: CLI display/output paths (triage/inbox/item/search/session context and related helpers), triage action output, and targeted tests.\\n- Verification: run focused vitest suites for touched command paths + kspec validate before submit.\",\"supersedes\":null},{\"_ulid\":\"01KJKJ64JHAYW893RNTS9CNKXC\",\"created_at\":\"2026-03-01T02:03:39.473Z\",\"author\":\"Jacob Chapel\",\"content\":\"Implemented shortest-unique ULID display refs across key CLI/export paths to prevent ambiguous 8-char prefixes from breaking copy/paste workflows.\\n\\nChanges:\\n- Added shared shortestUniqueUlid helper in parser refs and wired ReferenceIndex.shortUlid to use it.\\n- Updated triage/inbox/search/plan/item/session-context/session-checkpoint/log output paths to emit shortest unique refs instead of fixed 8-char prefixes in human-readable output.\\n- Updated shared triage action executor (CLI+daemon path) to disambiguate inbox refs and spec-gap observation result refs.\\n- Updated AC coverage matching logic (parser validate + task review) to accept variable ULID prefix lengths (8..full), preventing false uncovered-AC warnings when tests use shortest-unique refs.\\n- Updated HTML/context exports for tasks/items/triage records to emit disambiguated refs.\\n- Added regression test in tests/triage-cli.test.ts that seeds colliding triage ULIDs and verifies triage list prints distinct refs that each resolve via triage get.\\n\\nVerification:\\n- npm test -- tests/triage-cli.test.ts (56 passed)\\n- npm test -- tests/triage-actions.test.ts tests/observation-content-search.test.ts tests/cli-plan.test.ts tests/session-context.test.ts tests/validate-mode-selection.test.ts tests/item-list-under.test.ts tests/task-add-depends-on.test.ts (108 passed)\\n- kspec validate (fails with pre-existing project-wide meta/reference/alignment/completeness issues, including duplicate @observations slug and missing observations skill file)\",\"supersedes\":null},{\"_ulid\":\"01KJKJ74A1NSBDD9TB39QKSSHB\",\"created_at\":\"2026-03-01T02:04:11.970Z\",\"author\":\"Jacob Chapel\",\"content\":\"Opened PR #618: https://github.com/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pull/618 (branch fix/short-ulid-display-refs). Task submitted to pending_review.\",\"supersedes\":null},{\"_ulid\":\"01KJKK53PWW73JTYWWQGWM7V2V\",\"created_at\":\"2026-03-01T02:20:34.396Z\",\"author\":\"Jacob Chapel\",\"content\":\"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Review findings: SHOULD-FIX: duplicated shortestUniqueUlid implementations in src/export/html.ts and src/export/triage.ts instead of reusing shared src/parser/refs.ts helper (see PR #618 inline review comments).\",\"supersedes\":null}],\"todos\":[],\"automation\":\"eligible\",\"_sourceFile\":\"/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml\"}}\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"{\"success\":true,\"message\":\"Started task: 01KJDQ1D\",\"task\":{\"_ulid\":\"01KJDQ1DQMCBX32KDVWBJBF8W1\",\"slugs\":[],\"title\":\"ULID short ref ambiguity in batch operations: when two ULIDs share a prefix (e.g. 01KJ4SNE9 and 01KJ\",\"type\":\"task\",\"description\":\"ULID short ref ambiguity in batch operations: when two ULIDs share a prefix (e.g. 01KJ4SNE9 and 01KJ4SNEC), short refs like @01KJ4SNE fail. kspec already has a shortest-unique-ID utility — this should be used anywhere refs are displayed (triage list, task list, inbox list, promote result_ref, etc.) so that presented refs are always unambiguous and copy-pasteable into subsequent commands.\",\"spec_ref\":\"@batch-exec\",\"status\":\"in_progress\",\"blocked_by\":[],\"depends_on\":[],\"context\":[],\"priority\":3,\"tags\":[],\"vcs_refs\":[],\"session_id\":\"01KJKCGRAVN1BTZ611MX7EK5H3\",\"created_at\":\"2026-02-26T19:33:01.300Z\",\"started_at\":\"2026-03-01T02:22:52.837Z\"