/result command are always copy-pasteable into subsequent commands without ambiguity\\n\\n**Done when**:\\n- No occurrences of `_ulid.slice(0, 8)` remain in display-facing code paths\\n- All displayed refs (triage list, task list, inbox list, search results, promote result_ref, etc.) use `shortUlid()` or equivalent\\n- A test with two items sharing an 8-character ULID prefix shows that displayed refs are still unique and resolvable\",\"supersedes\":null},{\"_ulid\":\"01KJKHK2NRA76YCR98DKGTC5RR\",\"created_at\":\"2026-03-01T01:53:14.936Z\",\"author\":\"Jacob Chapel\",\"content\":\"Execution context:\\n- Background: displayed short refs currently use fixed 8-char ULID prefixes in many output paths; collisions make copy/paste refs ambiguous.\\n- Scope: update display-facing short-ref formatting to use shortest unique prefixes via ReferenceIndex (or equivalent local unique-set helper where index is unavailable) and add regression tests for ambiguous-prefix scenarios.\\n- Files: CLI display/output paths (triage/inbox/item/search/session context and related helpers), triage action output, and targeted tests.\\n- Verification: run focused vitest suites for touched command paths + kspec validate before submit.\",\"supersedes\":null},{\"_ulid\":\"01KJKJ64JHAYW893RNTS9CNKXC\",\"created_at\":\"2026-03-01T02:03:39.473Z\",\"author\":\"Jacob Chapel\",\"content\":\"Implemented shortest-unique ULID display refs across key CLI/export paths to prevent ambiguous 8-char prefixes from breaking copy/paste workflows.\\n\\nChanges:\\n- Added shared shortestUniqueUlid helper in parser refs and wired ReferenceIndex.shortUlid to use it.\\n- Updated triage/inbox/search/plan/item/session-context/session-checkpoint/log output paths to emit shortest unique refs instead of fixed 8-char prefixes in human-readable output.\\n- Updated shared triage action executor (CLI+daemon path) to disambiguate inbox refs and spec-gap observation result refs.\\n- Updated AC coverage matching logic (parser validate